0.392 0.455 0.545 rg
39.6850393700787407 754.0159842519684616 Td
(The Seat Locking Bracket is analysed as a progressive-die sheet-metal stamping per the forced classification. Geometry \(thin) Tj
T* (0.53-2.17mm walls, 1054 mostly line/bspline edges, and a large flat 255x226mm envelope\) is consistent with a stamped/formed bracket) Tj
T* (rather than a casting, despite the low fill ratio which is an artefact of the thin-shell sheet geometry. Because it is a seat-locking structural) Tj
T* (bracket \(safety-critical latch component\), high-strength steel \(mat-hss\) was selected over aluminium per the material default rule, giving a) Tj
T* (net part weight of 0.558kg. The 12-station \(1 blank + 15 bend\) progressive die costing £25,000 \(geometry-derived\) amortises efficiently) Tj
T* (across the 200,000 unit/year volume. Key manufacturability concerns are the 32 undercut faces \(needing cam-actuated forming\) and the) Tj
T* (unusually high free-form surface content \(235/426 faces\), both of which increase die complexity beyond a typical flat bracket stamping.) Tj
